+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BADIN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A porphyritic, horneblende-diorite and microdiorite, dolerite and olivine-augite hornblendite. Radiometric age: 458 +/- 9 Ma (K-AR whole rock) (Rundle, 1979)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BERG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Layered cumulate gabbros and quartz-gabbros, forming the Mosedale Intrusions which have a calc-alkaline/transitional to tholeiitic composition, microgabbro, microgranite with apatite-bearing iron-rich microdiorite, micromonzodiorite and microgranite zones forming the tholeiitic Carrock Intrusions, quartz-phyric rhyolite of the Harestones Rhyolite, and a microgranite named the Iron Crag Microgranite. Several component intrusions have Ordovician radiometric ages (Mosedale Gabbros, Carrock intrusions)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A microgabbro, cutting the main mass of micrographic microgranite, a narrow marginal zone of apatite-bearing, iron-rich gabbro, microdiorite, micromonzodiorite and microgranite. Radiometric age: microgranite 452.4 +/- 4.1 Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Millward and Evans, 2003)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CMGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRGD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRTO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Tonalite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Microgranodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Hornblendite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESK> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A pink, medium-grained muscovite granite, aphyric and porphyritic microgranite, coarse-grained granite, medium-grained granodiorite, microgranodiorite, biotite-rich granodiorite, and quartz-mica greisen locally containing topaz and quartz-andalusite rock associated with granite. The age of the granite is 450 +/- 3 Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Hughes et al., 1996)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/GALGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "This unit and the North England Subsuite (NEDP) encompass intrusions that occur to the north and south respectively of the Iapetus Suture trace."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LHTO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Several interconnected sill-like bodies of tonalite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MANXG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "All components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Isle of Man."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes all granite plutonic intrusions of Early Devonian age in Northern England, including the exposed Shap Pluton (SHAP), the Skiddaw Pluton (SKID) and the concealed Weardale and Crummock Water intrusions. The Shap Pluton is the type pluton for this Suite. \r\n\r\nThis unit and the Galloway Subsuite (GALGR) encompass intrusions that occur to the south and north respectively of the Iapetus Suture trace."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OTD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Microgabbro and granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/POGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PRTN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Sheets of dolerite and andesite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SGGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/THKD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A garnet-bearing, alkali feldspar-quartz-plagioclase-phyric microgranite. Age: 451.0 +/- 1.1 (2-sigma) Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Millward and Evans, 2003)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Not defined."@en .
